  "notes": "{出荷|しゅっか} refers to sending goods out from a warehouse or factory. It is a business/logistics term covering the dispatch side of the supply chain.\n\nFORMS:\n{出|しゅつ} (out) + {荷|か} (cargo, goods). Literally \"sending out the goods.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {出荷|しゅっか}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to ship\n- {出荷|しゅっか}⟦{準備|じゅんび}→準備：01431_junbi⟧: shipping preparation\n- {出荷|しゅっか}⟦{予定|よてい}→予定：00824_yotei⟧⟦{日|び}→日：02249_hi⟧: scheduled shipping date\n- {出荷|しゅっか}⟦{台数|だいすう}→台数：22482_daisuu⟧: number of units shipped\n- {出荷|しゅっか}⟦{停止|ていし}→停止：04067_teishi⟧: shipment suspension\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {出荷|しゅっか}: shipping out from warehouse/factory\n- ⟦{入荷|にゅうか}→入荷：07939_nyuuka⟧: arrival of goods (receiving stock)\n- ⟦{納品|のうひん}→納品：05134_nouhin⟧: delivery to the customer\n- ⟦{配送|はいそう}→配送：05464_haisou⟧: delivery, transport to destination\n- ⟦{発送|はっそう}→発送：10458_hassou⟧: dispatching (parcels, mail)",
